WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.190
Soak a bone in acid, and it turns
so bendy you can tie it in a knot.

2
00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.550
Heat an identical bone strongly,
and it crumbles at a touch.

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.660
Same bone, two opposite failures.

4
00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.840
Bone is not one material.

5
00:00:14.890 --> 00:00:18.320
It is a composite: two
materials in one tissue,

6
00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:20.540
like steel rods in concrete.

7
00:00:20.590 --> 00:00:24.670
So what do acid and heat reveal
about what bone is made of?

8
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.820
In this mission, you'll meet the living
cells that build bone up and break it

9
00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:30.800
down, all the time.

10
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:35.790
Then you'll zoom into compact bone, where
tiny canals bring blood within reach

11
00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:37.750
of every trapped cell.

12
00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.140
Your mission: explain what
soaking a bone in acid,

13
00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:43.730
and baking it, reveals about bone.
